{"id": "EUVD-2026-59287", "enisaUuid": "31f0e1d4-8662-3ac4-bc31-504a8ab1da4c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/panthor: Always use the IRQ-safe variant when acquiring the fence lock\n\nSince dma_fence objects can be shared with other subsystems, they may be\naccessed from hardirq context in those drivers, and we have to take\nthat into account by also using the IRQ-safe variant when acquiring\nthe lock.\n\nWhile at it, switch to the guard model.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1804a760422a7d75eb6e1fc0638aaff18d1dde88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9de9e8f279de0c299631f530de66c51642eef50a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2946aa6c97ac0e0d777baef8c0e6d944da8724a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/778c57d624974e64535ef1c9d9b4d8e5066153f4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72388", "GHSA-2vh6-fvwq-hq8w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00eb3a22-2f2a-3ab0-b545-2006b6169f77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "21614fbb-abc1-33f5-801a-d97ded98f236", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "2c1d6db3-2c9f-3e02-a30d-cef7fb0e00c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "6d9f83af-0292-30cd-956c-8e3a9bf4d0a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7b775fa6-3f18-3f60-8dc0-f9cb485201c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <1804a760422a7d75eb6e1fc0638aaff18d1dde88"}, {"id": "7e98c9f4-689a-3e57-8b73-98c72c0cdb03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "de85488138247d034eb3241840424a54d660926b <778c57d624974e6453